HST Office: every ribbon group launcher (↘) opens its own group's dialog on the group's tab, as in the reference
suite, instead of the tab used last.

- Writer: Phông chữ opens Character on Phông chữ; Đoạn văn (Trang đầu and Bố cục) opens Paragraph on Thụt lề và
  giãn cách; the table's Kiểu bảng opens Borders on Viền, its Căn chỉnh opens Table Properties on Bảng; the picture's
  Ảnh opens Picture on Kích thước, its Tô & viền on Đường viền (borders and shadow); the shape's Tô & viền opens Area on Vùng, its
  Định vị opens Position and Size on Vị trí và kích thước. Footnote/Endnote Settings (the Cước chú launcher)
  always opens on footnotes.
- Sheets: Phông chữ, Căn chỉnh and Số open Format Cells on Phông chữ, Căn chỉnh and Số; Tùy chọn trang tính (Page
  Setup on Trang tính, hst-sheets-sheet-options-launcher.patch) gets its caption as label too.
- Slides and Draw: Phông chữ opens Character on Phông chữ, Đoạn văn opens Paragraph on Thụt lề và giãn cách, Bản vẽ
  and Tô & viền open Area on Vùng, Đối tượng vẽ opens Position and Size on Vị trí và kích thước; Draw's Xoay và
  lật opens it on Xoay.
- The launchers send .uno:Command?Page:string=<tab id>. FormatArea, TransformDialog (svx), GraphicDialog,
  TableDialog (Writer) and FormatCellDialog (Sheets) get an optional Page argument. Where a handler reads any
  argument as "apply without a dialog", a Page argument that is the only one is taken out of the request first
  (sfx2/hstdialogpage.hxx), so every other call keeps its meaning. A launcher with a Page argument has no
  command label, so its .ui label is the group caption (same msgctxt, same translation).
- The bindings keep one dispatch per slot, made for the first URL; its state now also reaches listeners of the
  same command with other URL arguments (unoctitm.cxx). Without it, a launcher whose command also sits elsewhere
  on the tab with other arguments (or none) stayed disabled on the ribbon: Writer's table Căn chỉnh, picture and
  shape Tô và viền, shape Sắp xếp (seen on Windows; a dispatch from a test does not show it).

